    - id: 4
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: Didn't fight. Didn't break a rule. Didn't even raise my voice. Just
          failed their little math problem about bodies and boxes.
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 10
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 1
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "Tell me more \n\n[[Being trans in prison means you don\u2019t just
          do time \u2014 you get studied.\n\nAt intake, they ask the questions. Are
          you transgender? Have you been assaulted before? Do you think you\u2019re
          at risk? You can feel the room shift when you answer. From that point on,
          you\u2019re not just a person \u2014 you\u2019re a category.\n\nIn population,
          you\u2019re always aware of yourself. How you walk. How you talk. Who\u2019s
          watching. Some people leave you alone. Some don\u2019t. Staff might use
          the wrong name like it\u2019s nothing. Medical care turns into paperwork
          and waiting and hoping someone believes you.\n\nIf they decide you\u2019re
          \u201Ctoo vulnerable,\u201D they move you for \u201Cprotection.\u201D That
          usually means isolation. A locked door is still a locked door, even if
          they say it\u2019s for your own good.\n\nYou learn to calculate everything.
          Who\u2019s safe. When to correct someone. When to let it go. You get good
          at shrinking, or at standing still.\n\nMostly, it\u2019s exhausting.\nTrying
          to survive.\nTrying not to disappear.]]"
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: EventGuid
        value: 4c10509f-d07b-4ace-84c2-08a7ce72a9f2
        type: 0
        typeString: 
