    - id: 10
      fields:
      - title: Title
        value: Sneak a peek? Shoudn't that be accessible to us when we ask?
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Description
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Actor
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Conversant
        value: 2
        type: 5
        typeString: CustomFieldType_Actor
      - title: Menu Text
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Dialogue Text
        value: "Sneak a peek?\nThat\u2019s kind of the point \u2014 you\u2019re not
          really supposed to own it in here.\n\nYeah, it\u2019s supposed to be accessible
          when we ask. That\u2019s what they say. But \u2018accessible\u2019 usually
          means there\u2019s one copy somewhere in the unit office. Or on a cart.
          Or \u2018I\u2019ll bring it next round.\u2019\n\nIn SHU, you don\u2019t
          just walk to a shelf. You request it. You wait. If the officer\u2019s busy,
          short-staffed, or just not in the mood, it doesn\u2019t happen. And if
          you ask again too soon, now you\u2019re being pushy.\n\nEven when they
          do bring it, you get a few minutes standing at the door, trying to skim
          policies written in legal language that references three other policies
          you don\u2019t have.\n\nSo yeah \u2014 it should be accessible, but it's
          still a challenge."
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      - title: Sequence
        value: 
        type: 0
        typeString: 
      conversationID: 29
      isRoot: 0
      isGroup: 0
      nodeColor: 
      delaySimStatus: 0
